From: OpenWrt
Subject: ath10k: use direct firmware requests for optional probe files

With CONFIG_FW_LOADER_USER_HELPER_FALLBACK enabled, optional ath10k
firmware probes can trigger the sysfs/userspace firmware fallback and wait
for the global firmware loading timeout. This is especially visible during
boot when ath10k probes non-existent pre-calibration files, newer firmware
API files, and board API files before falling back to the files that are
actually present.

Use request_firmware_direct() for optional probe/fallback candidates so
missing files fail immediately. Keep the normal request path for the QCA988X
firmware API 5 file used by OpenWrt's qca988x firmware package, and for the
legacy board/calibration files that are actually consumed after optional
probes fail.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/core.c
@@ -934,8 +934,8 @@
 }
 
